---
import TextPage from '../layouts/TextPage.astro';
import Todo from '../components/Todo.astro';
import { book } from '../data/book';
import { legal, hosting } from '../data/legal';

const email = book.contactEmail;
---

<TextPage page="privacy" heading="Privacy policy" updated={legal.lastUpdated}>
  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>This website uses no cookies.</li>
    <li>It has no analytics, no advertising and no tracking.</li>
    <li>It has no forms and no accounts, so we don't ask you for any personal information.</li>
    <li>It doesn't collect personal information from children.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>
    {legal.publisherName || <Todo label="publisher's name" />}. Email: {email ? <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> : <Todo label="contact email" />}
  </p>

  <h2>What happens when you visit</h2>
  <p>
    Like every website, this one is delivered by computers that need some technical information to send you the page: your
    IP address, your browser type, the page you asked for and the time. Two companies handle this for us, on their own
    servers:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <b>{hosting.host.name}</b> hosts the website. GitHub logs visitors' IP addresses for security purposes. See
      <a href={hosting.host.privacy} target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub's privacy statement<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <b>{hosting.network.name}</b> delivers the website quickly and protects it from attacks. See
      <a href={hosting.network.privacy} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Cloudflare's privacy policy<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We don't use this information to identify you, build a profile of you, or show you ads. The fonts and pictures on this
    website are stored on the website itself, so your browser doesn't contact any other company to display them.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other websites</h2>
  <p>
    The Buy buttons take you to Amazon, and the video and social links take you to YouTube, Instagram, TikTok, Pinterest and
    Facebook. Nothing from those websites loads on this one until you click. Once you're on their website, their own
    privacy policy applies.
  </p>

  <h2>If you email us</h2>
  <p>
    If you write to {email ? <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> : 'us'}, we use your email address and message only to
    reply to you. We keep them only as long as we need to for that, and we never share or sell them.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    This website is made for children to enjoy with a grown-up. It doesn't ask children for any information. Buying the
    book happens on Amazon and is for grown-ups.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask us what personal information we hold about you (if any), and ask us to correct or delete it. Email
    {email ? <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> : 'us'} and we'll reply within one month. If you think we haven't
    handled your data properly, you can also complain to the data protection authority in your country.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If this website ever adds something that collects personal information, such as an email sign-up for the free
    printable page, this policy will be updated before it goes live. The date at the top shows the last change.
  </p>
</TextPage>
